WEBVTT

00:00:09.112 --> 00:00:10.952
(REPORTERS CLAMORING)

00:00:14.032 --> 00:00:15.192
REPORTER 1: McQueen, over here!

00:00:15.232 --> 00:00:17.192
REPORTER 2:
McQueen, how you feeling?

00:00:17.232 --> 00:00:18.872
Have you seen the latest
records Storm's been setting?

00:00:19.072 --> 00:00:20.552
Have you given any thought
to retirement?

00:00:21.032 --> 00:00:22.992
Okay, that's enough. No questions!

00:00:23.032 --> 00:00:24.392
Scusi. Out of the way!

00:00:24.712 --> 00:00:27.032
Coming through! Okay, back up.
Back up! No pictures. No, no, no.

00:00:28.072 --> 00:00:29.192
(CAMERAS CLICKING)

00:00:29.352 --> 00:00:31.232
Okay, thank you. Bye-bye.

00:00:31.912 --> 00:00:34.232
(SIGHS) Guido, can you believe them?

00:00:34.272 --> 00:00:35.872
Paparazzi. (SPITS)

00:00:37.432 --> 00:00:39.112
(CHUCKLES EXCITEDLY)

00:00:47.392 --> 00:00:48.472
Wow!

00:00:49.232 --> 00:00:50.632
DUSTY: Looks good, doesn't it?

00:00:50.792 --> 00:00:52.632
-Hey, guys.
-What do you think?

00:00:53.072 --> 00:00:55.072
What do I think? It's unbelievable.

00:00:55.232 --> 00:00:57.272
DUSTY: Yeah, you know,
it's kind of a cozy,

00:00:57.352 --> 00:00:59.072
humble, little place.

00:00:59.232 --> 00:01:01.232
Guys, how did you ever do this?

00:01:01.432 --> 00:01:03.872
-You want to tell him or should I?
-No, you start. Go ahead.

00:01:04.112 --> 00:01:07.192
(CLEARS THROAT)
We sold Rust-eze. Huh?

00:01:07.912 --> 00:01:08.912
What?

00:01:09.072 --> 00:01:12.152
What? You think a couple of jabronis
like us could do this on our own?

00:01:12.432 --> 00:01:14.552
-Wait. You sold Rust-eze?
-It's all good news.

00:01:14.712 --> 00:01:18.432
We just realized that you needed
something that we couldn't give you.

00:01:18.592 --> 00:01:20.952
It felt like the time
was right for us too.

00:01:21.112 --> 00:01:22.752
I mean, we're not as young
and handsome as we look.

00:01:22.792 --> 00:01:24.432
-(BOTH CHUCKLE)
-Oh, that's true.

00:01:24.672 --> 00:01:26.072
DUSTY: Besides, this Sterling fellow?

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.712
He's got every high-tech thing
you'll ever need.

00:01:28.872 --> 00:01:31.272
Everything we wanted to give you,
but couldn't.

00:01:31.592 --> 00:01:33.952
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Sterling? Who's Sterling?

00:01:34.112 --> 00:01:37.632
STERLING: Lightning McQueen!
You made some serious time, partner.

00:01:37.952 --> 00:01:39.592
Your new sponsor.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:42.552
He's the Mudflap King
of the Eastern seaboard.

00:01:42.792 --> 00:01:45.272
Welcome to the
Rust-eze Racing Center!

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:49.312
You have no idea how much
I've been looking forward to this.

00:01:49.472 --> 00:01:53.112
-Thanks, uh, Mr.--
-Please. No "mister". Just Sterling.

00:01:53.272 --> 00:01:55.032
I have been a fan of yours forever.

00:01:55.512 --> 00:01:57.512
And to be your sponsor?
How great is that?

00:01:57.592 --> 00:01:59.312
I can't thank
Rusty and Dusty here enough.

00:01:59.432 --> 00:02:00.992
Tough negotiators by the way.

00:02:01.152 --> 00:02:03.152
-Oh, you flatter us, but don't stop!
-(ALL LAUGHING)

00:02:03.952 --> 00:02:06.792
Anyway, just wanted to say
a quick hello.

00:02:06.792 --> 00:02:08.152
Take as much time as you need.

00:02:08.312 --> 00:02:09.552
Door's always open, guys.

00:02:12.312 --> 00:02:13.472
See?

00:02:22.952 --> 00:02:26.432
(SIGHS) I sure am gonna miss
racing for you guys.

00:02:28.472 --> 00:02:31.832
You know, you gave us
a lot of great memories, Lightning.

00:02:32.512 --> 00:02:34.352
Memories we'll remember.

00:02:34.792 --> 00:02:36.632
Wow. That's good.

00:02:38.352 --> 00:02:41.592
-Hey, Lightning, whatever you do--
-Don't drive like my brother!

00:02:41.752 --> 00:02:43.272
Don't drive like my brother.

00:02:43.352 --> 00:02:44.792
RUSTY: Please no pictures.

00:02:44.992 --> 00:02:47.112
DUSTY: Okay, maybe one.
Get my good side though, will you?

00:02:47.552 --> 00:02:48.912
(CHUCKLES)

00:02:54.312 --> 00:02:55.872
Whoa.

00:03:11.472 --> 00:03:13.192
STERLING: So? You like it?

00:03:13.472 --> 00:03:15.952
Oh, hey, Mr. Sterling. Wow.

00:03:16.752 --> 00:03:19.032
My career on a wall.

00:03:20.392 --> 00:03:22.072
Nice that you included Doc.

00:03:22.232 --> 00:03:24.632
Of course. He was your mentor.

00:03:25.512 --> 00:03:28.032
Losing him left a giant hole in the sport.

00:03:29.152 --> 00:03:30.352
Yeah.

00:03:32.072 --> 00:03:33.232
Jars of dirt?

00:03:33.472 --> 00:03:34.872
STERLING: Sacred dirt.

00:03:35.152 --> 00:03:38.552
Each of those jars contains dirt
from all the old tracks that Doc raced on.

00:03:38.752 --> 00:03:42.352
Florida International, Thunder Hollow,
just down the road and...

00:03:42.552 --> 00:03:44.992
our very own Fireball Beach,
right outside.

00:03:45.072 --> 00:03:46.032
McQUEEN: Huh.

00:03:47.672 --> 00:03:50.232
-Hey, is that--
-A bit of asphalt from Glen Ellen.

00:03:50.432 --> 00:03:51.552
My first win!

00:03:53.272 --> 00:03:54.672
You really are a fan.

00:03:54.872 --> 00:03:58.712
I am. And a fan of your future.

00:03:58.752 --> 00:03:59.872
You ready for it?

00:04:01.552 --> 00:04:02.872
Definitely.

00:04:03.552 --> 00:04:06.592
First, let's get you into a more...
contemporary look.

00:04:16.152 --> 00:04:17.232
Wow.

00:04:17.272 --> 00:04:18.752
STERLING ON SPEAKER:
It's an electronic suit.

00:04:18.952 --> 00:04:20.792
With it we'll be able to track your speed

00:04:20.832 --> 00:04:21.912
-and your vital signs.
-(BEEPING)

00:04:22.032 --> 00:04:23.272
Does it have a phone?

00:04:23.312 --> 00:04:26.072
(LAUGHS) Don't be crazy.
Racecars don't have phones.

00:04:27.592 --> 00:04:28.632
Wow.

00:04:28.712 --> 00:04:31.472
-Not bad, huh?
-This is really impressive.

00:04:31.552 --> 00:04:32.992
STERLING: This center has
quickly become

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:34.472
the most coveted destination...

00:04:34.552 --> 00:04:36.832
for young racers training
to make our team someday.

00:04:36.912 --> 00:04:39.712
And it's where you'll train
until you leave for Florida.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:43.472
Treadmills, wind tunnels, virtual reality.

00:04:43.632 --> 00:04:44.792
(THUDS)

00:04:45.152 --> 00:04:46.432
Still working on that.

00:04:46.592 --> 00:04:49.992
And the best fitness regimen
anyone could possibly imagine.

00:04:50.152 --> 00:04:54.192
Wait. Wait. Whoa. Is that the simulator?

00:04:54.432 --> 00:04:55.512
STERLING: Oh, yes.

00:04:55.592 --> 00:04:58.832
Lightning, I'd like to introduce
you to the multi-million dollar...

00:04:59.312 --> 00:05:01.472
flagship of interactive race simulation.

00:05:02.152 --> 00:05:06.312
The XDL 24-GTS Mark Z.

00:05:06.832 --> 00:05:11.352
The XDL... etcetera.

00:05:11.512 --> 00:05:14.152
Jackson Storm wishes
he had this model.

